Reflection is far more important than two-weaponing, save 2weapon for
later on when you have non-interfering reflection.  Spellcasting is
similar, although it can be worth taking more risks with the shield off
so long as you keep it on when you're going around corners and so forth
(and don't know what's back there).

Between those 2, that's 75% chance of getting reflection before meeting
dragons.

On top of that, presumably it's 50/50 on meeting a silver before a
black (although only 1/3 or so to get its scales, but /undead turning
can increase that), and around 50% chance of an early wish from a lamp
in minetown or other source (which may go for MR instead of reflection
depending on circumstances and whether Sokoban is done), and it's
certainly possible that none of the Castle dragons are black and you
can get the wand there, and shields/amulets of reflection do turn up
randomly.

I would be surprised if it's lower than 90% chance of reflection by the
time I meet a black dragon.

